1
00:00:01,528 --> 00:00:04,036
Daniel and Mei have a little boy, Kai.

2
00:00:04,036 --> 00:00:06,780
He is three, and their days are full.

3
00:00:07,803 --> 00:00:10,278
So they hire a live-in helper.

4
00:00:11,402 --> 00:00:13,593
Mya comes from Myanmar.

5
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:15,567
It is her first job,

6
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:18,058
and her English is limited.

7
00:00:19,169 --> 00:00:21,913
A translate app helps for a moment.

8
00:00:21,913 --> 00:00:24,258
The words come out in Burmese,

9
00:00:24,258 --> 00:00:25,824
then they are gone.

10
00:00:26,812 --> 00:00:28,790
Helper Diary keeps them.

11
00:00:28,908 --> 00:00:31,551
Daniel signs in first, as the owner.

12
00:00:34,458 --> 00:00:37,125
He invites Mei as an employer.

13
00:00:41,914 --> 00:00:44,036
She picks Chinese.

14
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:49,200
Then he invites Mya as the helper.

15
00:00:51,726 --> 00:00:55,495
She picks Burmese, and the whole app follows.

16
00:01:02,048 --> 00:01:02,779
On day one,

17
00:01:02,779 --> 00:01:05,876
Mei gives the usual brief in Talk.

18
00:01:08,398 --> 00:01:09,350
She just speaks,

19
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:11,681
and Mya reads it in Burmese.

20
00:01:14,873 --> 00:01:17,169
Mya types her answers back.

21
00:01:21,436 --> 00:01:23,442
Every talk is saved.

22
00:01:24,091 --> 00:01:25,984
The AI drafts the key points,

23
00:01:25,984 --> 00:01:27,792
and Daniel checks them.

24
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:35,472
Safety points, like Kai's allergy,

25
00:01:35,472 --> 00:01:37,113
go in straight away.

26
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,119
So Mya has a paper trail

27
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:46,756
in her own language,

28
00:01:46,756 --> 00:01:49,647
to read again whenever she is unsure.

29
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:57,357
For her week,

30
00:01:57,357 --> 00:02:00,640
Daniel asks the AI to write a routine.

31
00:02:04,258 --> 00:02:07,127
He checks it and puts it on the calendar.

32
00:02:12,903 --> 00:02:15,307
Mya ticks off her tasks on Today

33
00:02:15,307 --> 00:02:16,739
as she goes.

34
00:02:18,593 --> 00:02:21,624
Kai likes his bread with chocolate spread,

35
00:02:21,624 --> 00:02:23,455
cut into a circle.

36
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,859
In Kitchen, that is a photo

37
00:02:25,859 --> 00:02:28,476
she can look up instead of guessing.

38
00:02:32,746 --> 00:02:34,430
Mya keeps her own notes,

39
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:36,796
private until she shares them.

40
00:02:39,134 --> 00:02:42,207
Daniel can add to the Notebook any time.

41
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,621
When something is unclear,

42
00:02:49,621 --> 00:02:51,789
Mya asks in Burmese.

43
00:02:57,638 --> 00:02:59,702
Daniel answers in English,

44
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,401
and she reads it in Burmese.

45
00:03:09,867 --> 00:03:11,500
When Mya moves on,

46
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,098
Siti joins from Indonesia.

47
00:03:14,453 --> 00:03:17,100
The Notebook, the tasks and the Kitchen

48
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,594
are already there, in her language.

49
00:03:22,329 --> 00:03:24,663
Nobody repeats the brief.

50
00:03:25,992 --> 00:03:28,868
Helper Diary is open source.

51
00:03:29,225 --> 00:03:31,790
Each family runs its own copy,

52
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:33,230
with its own AI key,

53
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:35,116
and keeps its own data.

54
00:03:39,849 --> 00:03:42,904
Helper Diary is for the first few months,

55
00:03:42,904 --> 00:03:45,504
while your helper is still picking up English

56
00:03:45,504 --> 00:03:47,571
and your family is still learning

57
00:03:47,571 --> 00:03:49,173
how to work with her.

58
00:03:49,311 --> 00:03:51,087
It helps her settle in

59
00:03:51,087 --> 00:03:54,188
with less guessing and less frustration,

60
00:03:54,188 --> 00:03:56,252
for her and for you.

61
00:03:57,063 --> 00:03:59,850
If it might help your home too,

62
00:03:59,850 --> 00:04:01,867
look for helper-diary.
